{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"e05380bdbc70e3e423e1fa9a70ac9bd3896e87857d3f4de0a1c2c274337365d8","digest":{"component_or_area":"push recovery (dirty merge handling)","key_entities":["rebar._store.push_recovery._recover_dirty_merge","_merge_remote_under_lock","rebar._store.sync._untracked_overwrite_paths","_quarantine_untracked","git reset --hard","git merge --abort","_stash_create","reconverge-quarantine","_quarantine_dir_under","src/rebar/_store/push_recovery.py","src/rebar/_store/sync.py","tests/unit/test_push_recovery_untracked.py"],"problem_keywords":["untracked-overwrite","merge abort","recovery","wedge","push non-fast-forward","stash","quarantine"],"propositions":["Push recovery merge aborts when untracked local files collide with remote merge targets, causing repeated failures on retry with no self-healing mechanism.","The same untracked-overwrite wedge class (compaction-leftover files: *-SNAPSHOT.json, *.retired) that wedges reconverge also wedges push non-fast-forward recovery.","Recovery should quarantine colliding untracked paths into a shared directory and retry the merge once, reusing the sync module's parser and quarantine helpers.","Stash-recorded tracked edits must be restored exactly once on all exit paths (success, retry-failure, non-recoverable abort) without byte loss.","Genuine content conflicts and unnamed paths must preserve today's abort-and-restore behavior unchanged; quarantine moves only git-named colliding untracked files."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787398650994386001,"uuid":"9d8b6672-0ef9-4376-81e8-457276e8d0c7"}